"P1186176588" "Cyrus Thompson Taken"
// DetailString :
"P947763962" "One of the Thorns has dropped a yellowed slip of parchment detailing the shape and dimensions of the mystic symbols that must be drawn during the ceremony to bring their master to earth."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - MandyLebeaux 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2538114888" "Candy's Twin Sister"
// DetailString :
"P953364278" "Mandy Lebeaux is Candy Lebeaux's twin sister. They were working together at the fashion shoot in Atlas Park. She wasn't too happy to hear that you were there to rescue Candy, and failed."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - JimmyRemembers 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1952747771" "Jimmy Remembers"
// DetailString :
"P3316502624" "When Jimmy is thoroughly examined by Longbow medics later, it is found that he possesses a mutant gene that may well activate as he grows."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CandyRemembers 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2640477585" "Candy Remembers"
// DetailString :
"P791408550" "As you released Candy Lebeaux, you noticed an arcane symbol on her thigh. She was obviously destined to be part of some greater mystic event."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1611552184" "Smoke and Mirrors"
// DetailString :
"P2017302221" "Twilight's Son, the last of the Kheldians asks for your aid in finding an old retired hero by the name of Cyrus Thompson. He once went by the name of <color deepskyblue>Breakneck</color>. It's believed the Circle of Thorns seek Cyrus for some nefarious ceremony. You travel back in time to the Skyway City train station, hoping to find Cyrus. Yet, the Circle of Thorns had already collected him. Defeating the party of Thorns, you discover a yellowed slip of parchment, detailing mystic symbols used for a powerful ceremony."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3823046424" "Twilight's Son, the last of the Kheldians asks for your aid in finding an old retired hero by the name of Cyrus Thompson. He once went by the name of <color deepskyblue>Breakneck</color>. It's believed the Circle of Thorns seek Cyrus for some nefarious ceremony. You travel back in time to the Skyway City train station, hoping to find Cyrus. Yet, the Circle of Thorns had already collected him. Defeating the party of Thorns, you discover a yellowed slip of parchment, detailing mystic symbols used for a powerful ceremony.<br><br>With Cyrus gone, you return to Twilight's Son. He tells you that rather than going back again to find Cyrus, you should instead look for one of the other two potential victims: a boy named Jimmy Preston, hiding in an abandoned warehouse. The Circle of Thorns are already ahead of the game. You arrive too late again and see Jimmy as he's taken away."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission3Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P235655340" "Twilight's Son, the last of the Kheldians asks for your aid in finding an old retired hero by the name of Cyrus Thompson. He once went by the name of <color deepskyblue>Breakneck</color>. It's believed the Circle of Thorns seek Cyrus for some nefarious ceremony. You travel back in time to the Skyway City train station, hoping to find Cyrus. Yet, the Circle of Thorns had already collected him. Defeating the party of Thorns, you discover a yellowed slip of parchment, detailing mystic symbols used for a powerful ceremony.<br><br>With Cyrus gone, you return to Twilight's Son. He tells you that rather than going back again to find Cyrus, you should instead look for one of the other two potential victims: a boy named Jimmy Preston, hiding in an abandoned warehouse. The Circle of Thorns are already ahead of the game. You arrive too late again and see Jimmy as he's taken away.<br><br>Again Twilight's Son pushes you forward, rather than backwards in time. Sending you after the last of the 'cosmic keys' needed to perform this ceremony, a model named Candy Lebeaux. History tells of a fashion shoot in Atlas Park. The papers say that the shoot was interrupted by Circle of Thorns and many hostages were taken. This seemingly random event in the past now makes perfect sense. When you arrive, the courtyard is chaos. There are a number of hostages and after rescuing every one of them you discover that Candy is not among them."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SmokeAndMirrors 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// tDetailString :
"P374696051" "You hold an old tarnished belt buckle in the shape the letter B...<br><br>As you look at it, you remember Cyrus Thompson and his sacrifice. He dedicated his life helping people and he gave his live saving them. There's no greater hero than that.<br><br>It was Twilight's Son who sent you back in time to rescue him, Jimmy Preston and Candy Lebeaux from the Circle of Thorns. The Thorns were attempting to bring fourth their master from the nether realm and use those three as human sacrifices. Twilight's Son believed stopping this particular sacrifice was tied to the 'coming storm'. How? Twilight wouldn't say, 'it is the people of this time that can save your world'.<br><br>Saving people? You think back on this as you remember your last mission for him. You couldn't save them all. Just as you got there, you saw Cyrus Thompson get struck down trying to save the others. You managed to save the other two, but you'll never for get that old guy throwing himself into harms way.<br><br>The city put a statue up in front of the Kings Row train station, hopefully others will see him there and remember that being a hero is not how you dress or what powers you have, but who you help along the way."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - RequiemTimeTravelClue02H 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1026469962" "Dear {HeroName}..."
// DetailString :
"P1723866201" "While time traveling into the past, you visit Atlas Park and in a trashcan you find a hand written letter addressed to {HeroName}...<br><br>Once again, {HeroName}, it is rewarding to know that you are reading this antiquated form of communication. Have you rescued Candy's twin sister yet?  Not to worry, you will find Candy, Jimmy and even Cyrus very soon. But the busy work of Twilight's Son holds no interest for me.<br><br>I write to you because I believe that you have the ability to see beyond the smoke and mirrors placed around you. Silos talks of a coming conflict, but with whom? Has he told you or is he protecting his precious causality curve? I would like you to believe that Mender Silos is sending you back in time to change events in his favor, no one else's, but, that is something you may have to learn for yourself. Think on this, who benefits from these 'mends' that you do? Is it the people who are deemed unworthy to know the truth of what will happen to their race or is it someone else?<br><br>Before I go, I wish to reveal to you an ugly truth regarding Twilight's Son. He is, in fact, the last of his race, but that is because he sold the rest of his kind into slavery. Whether for his own gain or to escape their wrath, I do not know. Unfortunately for him, when the slave masters burned through the Kheldians, they came after him once more and he fled into the past. Perhaps he made yet another bargain with the masters, trading all the Kheldians of the past for his own survival.<br><br>Again, be cautious of those you speak to about this; the Menders are aware of my existence, but not my time or location and they would not take kindly to you associating with me. All I ask of you now is to do your duty, pursue the truth and look for more of my letters.<br><br>Travel well."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1603593416" "Hello, {HeroName}. I knew the time was right for you to seek me out. We have much work to do if we are to save this plane of existence. It is only with your help that we have a chance of setting things right, in this time and others. Steel yourself, hero, as what is to come will test every bit of your strength and resolve. For this task, you will be required to travel into the recent past and restore the natural order of the Chronoverse. <color orange>Your quest is to stop the Circle of Thorns from opening a portal to the netherworld and bringing their demonic master here to Earth</color>. If not, all is lost. You must seek out three individuals who serve as the 'cosmic key',  and keep them out of the Circle's evil hands. If they succeed... well, I can't bring myself to think of it...<br><br><color MediumOrchid>Editor's Note: Story and dialog written by City of Heroes' favorite comic book author Troy Hickman. This story was originally published in issues #4 - #6 of the City of Heroes comic book.</color>"
// AcceptString :
"P1715381550" "Protect Cyrus Thompson from the Circle of Thorns"
// SendOffString :
"P3160277769" "Are you familiar with the story of <color deepskyblue>Cyrus Thompson</color>, the hero once known as <color deepskyblue>Breakneck</color>? He and two others are the only means of bringing the demon to earth. <color>Go through the portal and find Cyrus and bring him back here</color>, that I might keep him safe.<br><br>If you can keep Cyrus out of their clutches, their master will forever be confined to his own nightmarish realm."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1790126182" "Protect Cyrus Thompson"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3953859945" "There is no time!  Find Cyrus Thompson so the world will not perish!"
// TaskTitle :
"P41831724" "<color deepskyblue>Smoke and Mirrors</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2039680635" "<color deepskyblue>Part One</color><br><color orange>Exemplar Level: 25 - 34</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2817334131" "Cyrus Thompson should be waiting outside of the Skyway City train station."

